    "title": "Sioux City Musketeers vs Adult Hockey League rematch - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Chase Foix Tyler Euchner Maren Ewertz ,\n40 minutes ago\nSIOUX CITY , Iowa ( KCAU ) ‚Äî It was a rematch between the Musketeers and the Sioux City Adult Hockey League to see who would take home the win.\nIn 2025, the Muskies and the Beer League faced off on the ice, with the Sioux City League beating the pros by just one point.\nThis year, the fight for the win took place at the Tyson Event Center, with the Sioux City Hockey League starting with 20 points.\nStory continues below\nHowever, the Muskies weren‚Äôt willing to lose quickly, scoring and catching up to the Adult League and beating them.\nWhile the Musketeers wanted to win, the teams were mostly looking forward to the fun.\n‚ÄúIt‚Äôs good for us because we get to take a break from an actual game,‚Äù said Shayne Gould, defense player for the Sioux City Musketeers. ‚ÄúYou know you don‚Äôt have to go 100%, but we‚Äôre still going to try, and it‚Äôs just good, good for us.‚Äù\nThe Muskies won 22-21 with the Sioux City Adult Hocket League only scoring one point on the Musketeers.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KCAU 9 News | Sioux City, IA | News, Weather, and Sports.",
